er example."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "The officials claim that this tax will result in a substantial increase in government revenues while affecting only the wealthy individuals and corporations who can afford to purchase such items.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is what the officials claim."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The tax will increase government revenues."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The increase will be substantial."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The tax will affect only certain people."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those are wealthy individuals."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Corporations are included too."}, {"n": 7, "text": "They are the ones who can afford such items."}]}], "the_read": "What if people will stop buying luxury goods once they are taxed, and the government will not generate any revenue?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q11", "qnum": 11, "question_type": "Evaluate", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 11, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q12", "prompt": "In a study of the relationship between aggression and television viewing in nursery school children, many interesting interactions among family styles, aggression, and television viewing were found. High aggression occurred in both high-viewing and low-viewing children and this seemed to be related to parental lifestyle. High-achieving, competitive, middle-class parents, whose children did not watch much television, had more aggressive children than parents who planned their lives in an organized, child-centered way, which included larger amounts of television viewing.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a study. · The study is of a relationship. · One side is aggression. · The other side is television viewing. · The subjects are nursery school children. (2) The study found interactions. · There were many of them. · They are described as interesting. · Family styles are one of the things involved. · Aggression is another of them. · Television viewing is another. (3) High aggression occurred in children. · It occurred in high-viewing children. · It also occurred in low-viewing children. · This seemed related to something. · What it related to is parental lifestyle. · This is a seeming rather than a certainty. (4) This is about a kind of parent. · Those parents are high-achieving. · Those parents are competitive. · They are middle-class. · Their children did not watch much television. (5) Those parents had more aggressive children. · The comparison is with another kind of parent. · Those others planned their lives. · The planning was organized. · It was also child-centered. · Their way included more television viewing.", "category": "Most Strongly Supported", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "In a study of the relationship between aggression and television viewing in nursery school children,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a study."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The study is of a relationship."}, {"n": 3, "text": "One side is aggression."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The other side is television viewing."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The subjects are nursery school children."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "many interesting interactions among family styles, aggression, and television viewing were found.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The study found interactions."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There were many of them."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They are described as interesting."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Family styles are one of the things involved."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Aggression is another of them."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Television viewing is another."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "High aggression occurred in both high-viewing and low-viewing children and this seemed to be related to parental lifestyle.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "High aggression occurred in children."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It occurred in high-viewing children."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It also occurred in low-viewing children."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This seemed related to something."}, {"n": 5, "text": "What it related to is parental lifestyle."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is a seeming rather than a certainty."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "High-achieving, competitive, middle-class parents, whose children did not watch much television,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a kind of parent."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Those parents are high-achieving."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those parents are competitive."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They are middle-class."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Their children did not watch much television."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "had more aggressive children than parents who planned their lives in an organized, child-centered way, which included larger amounts of television viewing.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Those parents had more aggressive children."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The comparison is with another kind of parent."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those others planned their lives."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The planning was organized."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It was also child-centered."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Their way included more television viewing."}]}], "the_read": "Television viewing alone cannot predict a child''s aggression.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q12", "qnum": 12, "question_type": "Most Strongly Supported", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 12, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q13", "prompt": "One of the effects of lead poisoning is an inflammation of the optic nerve, which causes those who have it to see bright haloes around light sources. In order to produce the striking yellow effects in his “Sunflowers” paintings, Van Gogh used Naples yellow, a pigment containing lead. Since in his later paintings, Van Gogh painted bright haloes around the stars and sun, it is likely that he was suffering from lead poisoning caused by ingesting the pigments he used.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about lead poisoning. · It names one of its effects. · T