round the stars and sun,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This gives a reason for what follows."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about his later paintings."}, {"n": 3, "text": "He painted haloes in them."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The haloes are bright."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They are around the stars."}, {"n": 6, "text": "They are around the sun as well."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "it is likely that he was suffering from lead poisoning caused by ingesting the pigments he used.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is stated as likely rather than certain."}, {"n": 3, "text": "He was suffering from lead poisoning."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The poisoning had a cause."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The cause is ingesting pigments."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The pigments are the ones he used."}]}], "the_read": "What if there wasn''t a high enough concentration of lead in the yellow paint to cause lead poisoning? What if many other things, like artistic creativity and second-hand accounts from lead-poisoning-sufferers, inspired the halos?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q13", "qnum": 13, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 13, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q14", "prompt": "Politician: The mandatory jail sentences that became law two years ago for certain crimes have enhanced the integrity of our system of justice, for no longer are there two kinds of justice, the kind dispensed by lenient judges and the kind dispensed by severe ones.\n\nPublic advocate: But with judges stripped of discretionary powers, there can be no leniency even where it would be appropriate. So juries now sometimes acquit a given defendant solely because the jurors feel that the mandatory sentence would be too harsh. Those juries, then, do not return an accurate verdict on the defendant’s guilt. This is why it is imperative that the legislation instituting mandatory jail sentences be repealed.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "