ed by lenient judges and the kind dispensed by severe ones.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This gives the reason for that claim."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There are no longer two kinds of justice."}, {"n": 3, "text": "One kind was dispensed by lenient judges."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The other was dispensed by severe judges."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Public advocate: But with judges stripped of discretionary powers, there can be no leniency even where it would be appropriate.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The second speaker is a public advocate."}, {"n": 2, "text": "This is a contrast with the politician."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Judges have been stripped of discretionary powers."}, {"n": 4, "text": "There can be no leniency."}, {"n": 5, "text": "That holds even where leniency would be appropriate."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "So juries now sometimes acquit a given defendant solely because the jurors feel that the mandatory sentence would be too harsh.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This follows from what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about juries."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They acquit a defendant."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This happens sometimes rather than always."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It is happening now."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The reason is the jurors'' feeling."}, {"n": 7, "text": "They feel the mandatory sentence would be too harsh."}, {"n": 8, "text": "That feeling is the sole reason."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those juries, then, do not return an accurate verdict on the defendant’s guilt.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This follows from what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about those juries."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They do not return an accurate verdict."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The verdict concerns the defendant''s guilt."}]}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is why it is imperative that the legislation instituting mandatory jail sentences be repealed.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It rests on what came before."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Something 