pe": "Most Strongly Supported", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 17, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q19", "prompt": "In the first decade following the founding of the British Labour party, the number of people regularly voting for Labour increased fivefold. The number of committed Labour voters increased a further fivefold during the party’s second decade. Since the increase was thus the same in the first as in the second decade, the often-made claim that the Labour party gained more voters in the party’s second decade than in its first is clearly false.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a decade. · The decade followed the founding of a party. · The party is the British Labour party. · It is about people voting for Labour. · Those people voted regularly. · Their number increased fivefold. (2) This is about committed Labour voters. · Their number increased again. · The increase was a further fivefold. · It happened during the second decade. · The decade is the party''s own second. (3) This gives a reason for what follows. · The increase is treated as the same in both decades. · The comparison is between the first and the second. (4) This is the conclusion. · It is about a claim other people make. · The claim is made often. · The claim is that Labour gained more voters in its second decade. · The comparison is with its first decade. · The conclusion says the claim is false. · It says so clearly.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "In the first decade following the founding of the British Labour party, the number of people regularly voting for Labour increased fivefold.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a decade."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The decade followed the founding of a party."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The party is the British Labour party."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It is about people voting for Labour."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those people voted regularly."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Their number increased fivefold."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "The number of committed Labour voters increased a further fivefold during the party’s second decade.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about committed Labour voters."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Their number increased again."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The increase was a further fivefold."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It happened during the second decade."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The decade is the party''s own second."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Since the increase was thus the same in the first as in the second decade,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This gives a reason for what follows."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The increase is treated as the same in both decades."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The comparison is between the first and the second."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "the often-made claim that the Labour party gained more voters in the party’s second decade than in its first is clearly false.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about a claim other people make."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The claim is made often."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The claim is that Labour gained more voters in its second decade."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The comparison is with its first decade."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The conclusion says the claim is false."}, {"n": 7, "text": "It says so clearly."}]}], "the_read": "What if a fivefold increase of a greater number is larger than a fivefold increase of a smaller number?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q19", "qnum": 19, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 18, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q20", "prompt": "A number of seriously interested amateur astronomers have tested the new Exodus refractor telescope. With it, they were able to observe in crisp detail planetary features that were seen only as fuzzy images in their 8-inch (approximately 20-centimeter) Newtonian telescopes, even though the 8-inch telescopes, with their wider apertures, gather more light than the 4-inch (approximately 10-centimeter) Exodus. Given these amateur astronomers’ observational findings, any serious amateur astronomer ought to choose the Exodus if she or he is buying a telescope for planetary observation.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about amateur astronomers. · They are seriously interested ones. · A number of them did something. · They tested a telescope. · The telescope is the Exodus refractor. · The telescope is new. (2) This is about using that telescope. · They were able to observe planetary features. · The detail was crisp. · The same features looked different before. · They were seen only as fuzzy images. · That was in their Newtonian telescopes. · Those telescopes are 8-inch ones. · Eight inches is about 20 centimeters. (3) This is a contrast with what came before. · It is about the 8-inch telescopes. · Those telescopes have wider apertures. · They gather more light. · The comparison is with the Exodus. · The Exodus is a 4-inch telescope. · Four inches is about 10 centimeters. (4) This is the conclusion. · It rests on those observational findings. · The findings belong to these amateur astronomers. · It is about any serious amateur astronomer. · Such a person ought to choose the Exodus. · This applies under a condition. · The condition is buying a telescope for planetary observation.", "category": "Method", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "A number of seriously interested amateur astronomers have tested the new Exodus refractor telescope.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about amateur astronomers."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They are seriously interested ones."}, {"n": 3, "text": "A number of them did something."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They tested a telescope."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The telescope is the Exodus refractor."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The telescope is new."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "With it, they were able to observe in crisp detail planetary features that were seen only as fuzzy images in their 8-inch (approximately 20-centimeter) Newtonian telescopes,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about using that telescope."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They were able to observe planetary features."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The detail was crisp."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The same features looked different before."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They were seen only as fuzzy images."}, {"n": 6, "text": "That was in their Newtonian telescopes."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Those telescopes are 8-inch ones."}, {"n": 8, "text": "Eight inches is about 20 centimeters."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "even though the 8-inch telescopes, with their wider apertures, gather more light than the 4-inch (approximately 10-centimeter) Exodus.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about the 8-inch telescopes."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those telescopes have wider apertures."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They gather more light."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The comparison is with the Exodus."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The Exodus is a 4-inch telescope."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Four inches is about 10 centimeters."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Given these amateur astronomers’ observational findings, any serious amateur astronomer ought to choose the Exodus if she or he is buying a telescope for planetary observation.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It rests on those observational findings."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The findings belong to these amateur astronomers."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It is about any serious amateur astronomer."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Such a person ought to choose the Exodus."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This applies under a condition."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The condition is buying a telescope for planetary observation."}]}], "the_read": "What if there''s a downside to Exodus refractor telescopes? What if it''s too expensive for any amateur?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q20", "qnum": 20, "question_type": "Method", "correct_answer": "D"}, {"citation": "PT21.S3.Q21", "qnum": 21, "question_type": "Weaken", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 19, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q22", "prompt": "Anatomical bilateral symmetry is a common trait. It follows, therefore, that it confers survival advantages on organisms. After all, if bilateral symmetry did not confer such advantages, it would not be common.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a trait. · The trait is anatomical bilateral symmetry. · The trait is common. (2) This is the conclusion. · It is drawn from what came before. · The symmetry confers advantages. · The advantages are survival advantages. · They are conferred on organisms. (3) This supports the conclusion. · It is a conditional statement. · The condition is symmetry not conferring such advantages. · In that case it would not be common.", "category": "Parallel Reasoning", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Anatomical bilateral symmetry is a common trait.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a trait."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The trait is anatomical bilateral symmetry."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The trait is common."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "It follows, therefore, that it confers survival advantages on organisms.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is drawn from what came before."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The symmetry confers advantages."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The advantages are survival advantages."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They are conferred on organisms."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "After all, if bilateral symmetry did not confer such advantages, it would not be common.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This supports the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is a conditional statement."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The condition is symmetry not conferring such advantages."}, {"n": 4, "text": "In that case it would not be common."}]}], "the_read": "What if the rules of conditional reasoning don''t apply?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q22", "qnum": 22, "question_type": "Parallel Reasoning", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 20, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q23", "prompt": "Electrical engineers have repeatedly demonstrated that the best solid-state amplifiers are indistinguishable from the best vacuum-tube amplifiers with respect to the characteristics commonly measured in evaluating the quality of an amplifier’s musical reproduction. Therefore, those music lovers who insist that recorded music sounds better when played with the best vacuum-tube amplifier than when played with the best solid-state amplifier must be imagining the difference in quality that they claim to hear.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about electrical engineers. · They have demonstrated something repeatedly. · It concerns the best solid-state amplifiers. · Those are indistinguishable from the best vacuum-tube amplifiers. · The indistinguishability is limited to certain characteristics. · Those characteristics are the ones commonly measured. · They are measured to evaluate quality. · The quality is of musical reproduction. (2) This is the conclusion. · It is about certain music lovers. · Those people insist on something. · They say recorded music sounds better with a vacuum-tube amplifier. · The comparison is with the best solid-state amplifier. · The conclusion says they must be imagining it. · What they imagine is the difference in quality. · It is a difference they claim to hear.", "category": "Weaken", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Electrical engineers have repeatedly demonstrated that the best solid-state amplifiers are indistinguishable from the best vacuum-tube amplifiers with respect to the characteristics commonly measured in evaluating the quality of an amplifier’s musical reproduction.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about electrical engineers."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They have demonstrated something repeatedly."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It concerns the best solid-state amplifiers."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Those are indistinguishable from the best vacuum-tube amplifiers."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The indistinguishability is limited to certain characteristics."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Those characteristics are the ones commonly measured."}, {"n": 7, "text": "They are measured to evaluate quality."}, {"n": 8, "text": "The quality is of musical reproduction."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Therefore, those music lovers who insist that recorded music sounds better when played with the best vacuum-tube amplifier than when played with the best solid-state amplifier must be imagining the difference in quality that they claim to hear.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about certain music lovers."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those people insist on something."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They say recorded music sounds better with a vacuum-tube amplifier."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The comparison is with the best solid-state amplifier."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The conclusion says they must be imagining it."}, {"n": 7, "text": "What they imagine is the difference in quality."}, {"n": 8, "text": "It is a difference they claim to hear."}]}], "the_read": "What if they are distinguishable with respect to characteristics not commonly measured?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q23", "qnum": 23, "question_type": "Weaken", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 21, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q24", "prompt": "Explanation must be distinguished from justification. Every human action potentially has an explanation; that is, with sufficient knowledge it would be possible to give an accurate description of the causes of that action. An action is justified only when the person performing the action has sufficient reasons for the action. According to many psychologists, even when there is a justification for an action, that justification often forms no part of the explanation. The general principle, however, is that only an action whose justification, that is, the reasons for the action, forms an essential part of its explanation is rational.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about two things. · One of them is explanation. · The other is justification. · The two must be distinguished. (2) This is about every human action. · Each one potentially has an explanation. · The rest restates what that means. · Sufficient knowledge would be needed. · It would be possible to give a description. · The description would be accurate. · What is described is the causes of the action. (3) This is about when an action is justified. · It states a necessary condition. · The person performing the action must have reasons. · The reasons must be sufficient. (4) This is attributed to psychologists. · It is the view of many of them. · It applies even when a justification exists. · The justification forms no part of the explanation. · This is often so rather than always. (5) This is a contrast with what came before. · It states a general principle. · The principle is about which actions are rational. · An action''s justification is its reasons. · Those reasons must form part of its explanation. · The part must be an essential one. · Only such an action is rational.", "category": "Inference", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Explanation must be distinguished from justification.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about two things."}, {"n": 2, "text": "One of them is explanation."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The other is justification."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The two must be distinguished."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Every human action potentially has an explanation; that is, with sufficient knowledge it would be possible to give an accurate description of the causes of that action.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about every human action."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Each one potentially has an explanation."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The rest restates what that means."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Sufficient knowledge would be needed."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It would be possible to give a description."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The description would be accurate."}, {"n": 7, "text": "What is described is the causes of the action."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "An action is justified only when the person performing the action has sufficient reasons for the action.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about when an action is justified."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It states a necessary condition."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The person performing the action must have reasons."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The reasons must be sufficient."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "According to many psychologists, even when there is a justification for an action, that justification often forms no part of the explanation.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is attributed to psychologists."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is the view of many of them."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It applies even when a justification exists."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The justification forms no part of the explanation."}, {"n": 5, "text": "This is often so rather than always."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "The general principle, however, is that only an action whose justification, that is, the reasons for the action, forms an essential part of its explanation is rational.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast with what came before."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It states a general principle."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The principle is about which actions are rational."}, {"n": 4, "text": "An action''s justification is its reasons."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those reasons must form part of its explanation."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The part must be an essential one."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Only such an action is rational."}]}], "the_read": "According to many psychologists, there are some human actions that are not rational.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q24", "qnum": 24, "question_type": "Inference", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 22, "slug": "PT21_S3_Q25", "prompt": "At the company picnic, all of the employees who participated in more than four of the scheduled events, and only those employees, were eligible for the raffle held at the end of the day. Since only a small proportion of the employees were eligible for the raffle, most of the employees must have participated in fewer than four of the scheduled events.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about a company picnic. · It is about employees. · Those employees participated in scheduled events. · They participated in more than four of them. (2) This limits the group to those employees only. · Those employees were eligible for something. · What they were eligible for is a raffle. · The raffle was held at the end of the day. (3) This is the conclusion. · It rests on a given. · The given is that few employees were eligible. · The proportion eligible was small. · The conclusion is about most of the employees. · They must have participated in fewer than four events. · The events are the scheduled ones.", "category": "Parallel Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "At the company picnic, all of the employees who participated in more than four of the scheduled events,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about a company picnic."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about employees."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those employees participated in scheduled events."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They participated in more than four of them."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "and only those employees, were eligible for the raffle held at the end of the day.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This limits the group to those employees only."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Those employees were eligible for something."}, {"n": 3, "text": "What they were eligible for is a raffle."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The raffle was held at the end of the day."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Since only a small proportion of the employees were eligible for the raffle, most of the employees must have participated in fewer than four of the scheduled events.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It rests on a given."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The given is that few employees were eligible."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The proportion eligible was small."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The conclusion is about most of the employees."}, {"n": 6, "text": "They must have participated in fewer than four events."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The events are the scheduled ones."}]}], "the_read": "What if most employees participated in exactly four events?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT21.S3.Q25", "qnum": 25, "question_type": "Parallel Flaw", "correct_answer": "E"}]}]'::jsonb,
