mall."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The percentage is of the total amount of the outstanding bills."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "a company interested in reducing losses from long-outstanding bills would be well advised to pursue its debtors on its own.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about a company interested in reducing losses."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The losses come from long-outstanding bills."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Such a company would be well advised to pursue its debtors."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It should pursue them on its own."}]}], "the_read": "What if it''s much more expensive to pursue debtors on your own? What if at least with collections there''s a guarantee you''ll get some money?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q13", "qnum": 13, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 12, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q14", "prompt": "Herbalist: Many of my customers find that their physical coordination improves after drinking juice containing certain herbs. A few doctors assert that the herbs are potentially harmful, but doctors are always trying to maintain a monopoly over medical therapies. So there is no reason not to try my herb juice.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) A herbalist is speaking. · Many of his customers find something. · Their physical coordination improves. · The improvement follows drinking juice. · The juice contains certain herbs. (2) Some doctors make an assertion. · Only a few do. · They say the herbs are potentially harmful. · This is a contrast. · Doctors try to maintain a monopoly. · The monopoly is over medical therapies. · They always do this. (3) This is the conclusion. · There is no reason against it. · What there is no reason against is trying his herb juice.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Herbalist: Many of my customers find that their physical coordination improves after drinking juice containing certain herbs.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "A herbalist is speaking."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Many of his customers find something."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Their physical coordination improves."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The improvement follows drinking juice."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The juice contains certain herbs."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "A few doctors assert that the herbs are potentially harmful, but doctors are always trying to maintain a monopoly over medical therapies.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Some doctors make an assertion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Only a few do."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They say the herbs are potentially harmful."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Doctors try to maintain a monopoly."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The monopoly is over medical therapies."}, {"n": 7, "text": "They always do this."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "So there is no reason not to try my herb juice.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There is no reason against it."}, {"n": 3, "text": "What there is no reason against is trying his herb juice."}]}], "the_read": "What if just because doctors want a monopoly that doesn''t mean they''re wrong about herb danger?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT102.S3.Q14", "qnum": 14, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 13, "slug": "PT102_S3_Q15", "prompt": "Because of the lucrative but illegal trade in rhinoceros horns, a certain rhinoceros species has been hunted nearly to extinction. Therefore an effective way to ensure the survival of that species would be to periodically trim off the horns of all rhinoceroses, thereby eliminating the motivation for poaching.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is the reason given. · There is a trade in rhinoceros horns. · The trade is lucrative. · The trade is illegal. · A 