other color. · This is an overall figure. (3) This is conditional on the claim being true. · The conclusion is that lives could be saved. · The way to save them is banning red cars. · The ban would remove them from the roads. · The ban would be total, not partial. · The claim is made with certainty.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Premiums for automobile accident insurance are often higher for red cars than for cars of other colors.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about insurance premiums."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The insurance is automobile accident insurance."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Premiums are higher for red cars."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The comparison is with cars of other colors."}, {"n": 5, "text": "This is often the case."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "To justify these higher charges, insurance companies claim that, overall, a greater percentage of red cars are involved in accidents than are cars of any other color.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Insurance companies want to justify the charges."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They make a claim."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The claim is about a percentage."}, {"n": 4, "text": "A greater percentage of red cars are involved in accidents."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The comparison is with cars of any other color."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is an overall figure."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "If this claim is true, then lives could undoubtedly be saved by banning red cars from the roads altogether.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is conditional on the claim being true."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The conclusion is that lives could be saved."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The way to save them is banning red cars."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The ban would remove them from the roads."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The ban would be total, not partial."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The claim is made with certainty."}]}], "the_read": "What if the color red does not cause the accidents? What if red cars tend to get in more accidents because reckless drivers tend to choose red cars?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q10", "qnum": 10, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 11, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q11", "prompt": "A certain credit-card company awards its customers bonus points for using its credit card. Customers can use accumulated points in the purchase of brand name merchandise by mail at prices lower than the manufacturers'' suggested retail prices. At any given time, therefore, customers who purchase merchandise using the bonus points spend less than they would spend if they purchased the same merchandise in retail stores.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) There is a credit-card company. · It awards bonus points. · The points go to its customers. · They are awarded for using its credit card. (2) Customers accumulate the points. · They can use them to purchase merchandise. · The merchandise is brand name. · The purchase is by mail. · The prices are lower. · The comparison is with manufacturers'' suggested retail prices. (3) This is the conclusion. · It holds at any given time. · It is about customers who purchase using the bonus points. · Those customers spend less money. · The comparison is with what they would otherwise spend. · The alternative is buying the same merchandise in retail stores.", "category": "Necessary Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "A certain credit-card company awards its customers bonus points for using its credit card.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "There is a credit-card company."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It awards bonus points."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The points go to its customers."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They are awarded for using its credit card."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Customers can use accumulated points in the purchase of brand name merchandise by mail at prices lower than the manufacturers'' suggested retail prices.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Customers accumulate 