hey are fed breast milk exclusively.", "category": "Weaken", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "It is probably not true that colic in infants is caused by the inability of those infants to tolerate certain antibodies found in cow''s milk,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is hedged as probably not true."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The claim being rejected is about colic in infants."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The claim is that colic is caused by an inability."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The inability is to tolerate certain antibodies."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Those antibodies are found in cow''s milk."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "since it is often the case that symptoms of colic are shown by infants that are fed breast milk exclusively.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the reason."}, {"n": 2, "text": "This is often the case."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Symptoms of colic are shown."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They are shown by infants."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those infants are fed breast milk."}, {"n": 6, "text": "They are fed breast milk exclusively."}]}], "the_read": "What if cow''s milk and breast milk contain the same antibodies? What if colic can have multiple causes?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q12", "qnum": 12, "question_type": "Weaken", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 13, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q13", "prompt": "Yolanda: Gaining access to computers without authorization and manipulating the data and programs they contain is comparable to joyriding in stolen cars; both involve breaking into private property and treating it recklessly. Joyriding, however, is the more dangerous crime because it physically endangers people, whereas only intellectual property is harmed in the case of computer crimes.\n\nArjun: I disagree! For example, unauthorized use of medical records systems in hospitals could damage data systems on which human lives depend, and therefore computer crimes also cause physical harm to people.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Yolanda is the first speaker. · She describes gaining access to computers. · The access is without authorization. · It also includes manipulating data and programs. · Those are what the computers contain. · She compares this to joyriding. · The joyriding is in stolen cars. (2) This is what the two share. · Both involve breaking in. · What is broken into is private property. · Both involve treating it recklessly. (3) This is a contrast. · Joyriding is the more dangerous of the two. · The reason is that it endangers people. · The danger is physical. · With computer crimes only intellectual property is harmed. (4) A second speaker begins. · The speaker is Arjun. · Arjun disagrees with what Yolanda said. (5) This is his example. · It is unauthorized use. · The use is of medical records systems. · Those systems are in hospitals. · Such use could damage data systems. · Human lives depend on those systems. (6) This is his conclusion. · It is about computer crimes. · They cause physical harm. · The harm is to people. · They do this too, not only joyriding.", "category": "Controversy", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Yolanda: Gaining access to computers without authorization and manipulating the data and programs they contain is comparable to joyriding in stolen cars;", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Yolanda is the first speaker."}, {"n": 2, "text": "She describes gaining access to computers."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The access is without authorization."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It also includes manipulating data and programs."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Those are what the computers contain."}, {"n": 6, "text": "She compares this to joyriding."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The joyriding is in stolen cars."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "both involve breaking into private property and treating it recklessly.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is what the two share."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Both involve breaking in."}, {"n": 3, "text": "What is broken into is private property."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Both involve treating it recklessly."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Joyriding, however, is the more dangerous crime because it physically endangers people, whereas only intellectual property is harmed in the case of computer crimes.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Joyriding is the more dangerous of the two."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The reason is that it endangers people."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The danger is physical."}, {"n": 5, "text": "With computer crimes only intellectual property is harmed."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Arjun: I disagree!", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "A second speaker begins."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The speaker is Arjun."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Arjun disagrees with what Yolanda said."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "For example, unauthorized use of medical records systems in hospitals could damage data systems on which human lives depend,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is his example."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is unauthorized use."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The use is of medical records systems."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Those systems are in hospitals."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Such use could damage data systems."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Human lives depend on those systems."}]}, {"n": 6, "text": "and therefore computer crimes also cause physical harm to people.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is his conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about computer crimes."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They cause physical harm."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The harm is to people."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They do this too, not only joyriding."}]}], "the_read": "The speakers disagree over whether computer crimes only ever cause harm to intellectual property.", "the_read_type": "C", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q13", "qnum": 13, "question_type": "Controversy", "correct_answer": "D"}, {"citation": "PT105.S2.Q14", "qnum": 14, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 14, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q15", "prompt": "A report of a government survey concluded that Center City was among the ten cities in the nation with the highest dropout rate from its schools. The survey data were obtained by asking all city residents over the age of 19 whether they were high school graduates and computing the proportion who were not. A city school official objected that the result did not seem accurate according to the schools'' figures.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) There is a report. · The report is of a government survey. · It reached a conclusion. · The conclusion is about Center City. · Center City was among ten cities. · Those ten had the highest dropout rate. · The rate is from its schools. · The comparison is nationwide. (2) This is how the data were obtained. · People were asked a question. · Those asked were all city residents. · They were over the age of 19. · The question was whether they were high school graduates. · A proportion was then computed. · The proportion was of those who were not. (3) Someone raised an objection. · The objector is a city school official. · The objection is that the result did not seem accurate. · The basis is the schools'' own figures.", "category": "Gap Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "A report of a government survey concluded that Center City was among the ten cities in the nation with the highest dropout rate from its schools.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "There is a report."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The report is of a government survey."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It reached a conclusion."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The conclusion is about Center City."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Center City was among ten cities."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Those ten had the highest dropout rate."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The rate is from its schools."}, {"n": 8, "text": "The comparison is nationwide."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "The survey data were obtained by asking all city residents over the age of 19 whether they were high school graduates and computing the proportion who were not.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is how the data were obtained."}, {"n": 2, "text": "People were asked a question."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those asked were all city residents."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They were over the age of 19."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The question was whether they were high school graduates."}, {"n": 6, "text": "A proportion was then computed."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The proportion was of those who were not."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "A city school official objected that the result did not seem accurate according to the schools'' figures.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Someone raised an objection."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The objector is a city school official."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The objection is that the result did not seem accurate."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The basis is the schools'' own figures."}]}], "the_read": "What if many of the residents over 19 had gone and dropped out of school in another city? What if most people who didn''t finish high school were expelled?", "the_read_type": "R", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q15", "qnum": 15, "question_type": "Gap Flaw", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 15, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q16", "prompt": "Brown dwarfs—dim red stars that are too cool to burn hydrogen—are very similar in appearance to red dwarf stars, which are just hot enough to burn hydrogen. Stars, when first formed, contain substantial amounts of the element lithium. All stars but the coolest of the brown dwarfs are hot enough to destroy lithium completely by converting it to helium. Accordingly, any star found that contains no lithium is not one of these coolest brown dwarfs.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Brown dwarfs are stars. · They are dim and red. · They are too cool to burn hydrogen. · They look very similar to red dwarf stars. · Red dwarfs are just hot enough to burn hydrogen. (2) This is about stars when first formed. · Newly formed stars contain lithium. · The amounts are substantial. (3) Almost all stars are hot enough to destroy lithium. · The exception is the coolest of the brown dwarfs. · The destruction is complete. · It happens by converting lithium to helium. (4) This is the conclusion. · It is about any star found to contain no lithium. · Such a star is not one of these coolest brown dwarfs.", "category": "Necessary Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Brown dwarfs—dim red stars that are too cool to burn hydrogen—are very similar in appearance to red dwarf stars, which are just hot enough to burn hydrogen.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Brown dwarfs are stars."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They are dim and red."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They are too cool to burn hydrogen."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They look very similar to red dwarf stars."}, {"n": 5, "text": "Red dwarfs are just hot enough to burn hydrogen."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Stars, when first formed, contain substantial amounts of the element lithium.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about stars when first formed."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Newly formed stars contain lithium."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The amounts are substantial."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "All stars but the coolest of the brown dwarfs are hot enough to destroy lithium completely by converting it to helium.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Almost all stars are hot enough to destroy lithium."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The exception is the coolest of the brown dwarfs."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The destruction is complete."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It happens by converting lithium to helium."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Accordingly, any star found that contains no lithium is not one of these coolest brown dwarfs.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about any star found to contain no lithium."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Such a star is not one of these coolest brown dwarfs."}]}], "the_read": "What if at one point in their lives the coolest brown dwarfs were hot enough to burn lithium? What if the coolest brown dwarfs were not always this way?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q16", "qnum": 16, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 16, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q17", "prompt": "Whenever a company loses a major product-liability lawsuit, the value of the company''s stocks falls significantly within hours after the announcement. Cotoy has long been involved in a major product-liability lawsuit, and its stocks fell significantly in value today. Therefore, we can be sure that an unfavorable judgment against Cotoy in that lawsuit was announced earlier today.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is a rule about companies. · The trigger is losing a lawsuit. · The lawsuit is a major product-liability one. · The company''s stock value falls. · The fall is significant. · It happens within hours. · It happens after the announcement. (2) Cotoy is involved in a lawsuit. · The lawsuit is a major product-liability one. · The involvement has been long. · Cotoy''s stocks fell. · The fall was significant. · The fall happened today. (3) This is the conclusion. · It is stated with certainty. · A judgment was announced. · The judgment was unfavorable. · It was against Cotoy. · It was in that lawsuit. · The announcement was earlier today.", "category": "Parallel Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Whenever a company loses a major product-liability lawsuit, the value of the company''s stocks falls significantly within hours after the announcement.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a rule about companies."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The trigger is losing a lawsuit."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The lawsuit is a major product-liability one."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The company''s stock value falls."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The fall is significant."}, {"n": 6, "text": "It happens within hours."}, {"n": 7, "text": "It happens after the announcement."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Cotoy has long been involved in a major product-liability lawsuit, and its stocks fell significantly in value today.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Cotoy is involved in a lawsuit."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The lawsuit is a major product-liability one."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The involvement has been long."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Cotoy''s stocks fell."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The fall was significant."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The fall happened today."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "Therefore, we can be sure that an unfavorable judgment against Cotoy in that lawsuit was announced earlier today.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is stated with certainty."}, {"n": 3, "text": "A judgment was announced."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The judgment was unfavorable."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It was against Cotoy."}, {"n": 6, "text": "It was in that lawsuit."}, {"n": 7, "text": "The announcement was earlier today."}]}], "the_read": "What if other situations can cause a company''s stocks to fall significantly in value? What if we can''t use bad conditional reasoning?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q17", "qnum": 17, "question_type": "Parallel Flaw", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 17, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q18", "prompt": "In recent years the climate has been generally cool in northern Asia. But during periods when the average daily temperature and humidity in northern Asia were slightly higher than their normal levels the yields of most crops grown there increased significantly. In the next century, the increased average daily temperature and humidity attained during those periods are expected to become the norm. Yet scientists predict that the yearly yields of most of the region''s crops will decrease during the next century.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about recent years. · The place is northern Asia. · The climate there has been generally cool. (2) This is a contrast. · There were periods of higher temperature and humidity. · The measure is the average daily level. · The rise above normal was slight. · The yields of crops increased. · The increase was significant. · It applied to most crops grown there. (3) This is about the next century. · Those higher levels are expected to become the norm. · They are the levels reached during those periods. (4) This is the puzzle. · Scientists make a prediction. · The yields will decrease. · The yields are yearly. · It applies to most of the region''s crops. · This is during the next century.", "category": "Resolution", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "In recent years the climate has been generally cool in northern Asia.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about recent years."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The place is northern Asia."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The climate there has been generally cool."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "But during periods when the average daily temperature and humidity in northern Asia were slightly higher than their normal levels the yields of most crops grown there increased significantly.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There were periods of higher temperature and humidity."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The measure is the average daily level."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The rise above normal was slight."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The yields of crops increased."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The increase was significant."}, {"n": 7, "text": "It applied to most crops grown there."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "In the next century, the increased average daily temperature and humidity attained during those periods are expected to become the norm.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about the next century."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Those higher levels are expected to become the norm."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They are the levels reached during those periods."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Yet scientists predict that the yearly yields of most of the region''s crops will decrease during the next century.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the puzzle."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Scientists make a prediction."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The yields will decrease."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The yields are yearly."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It applies to most of the region''s crops."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is during the next century."}]}], "the_read": "What if sustained high temperatures will cause an increase in crop pests?", "the_read_type": "R", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q18", "qnum": 18, "question_type": "Resolution", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 18, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q19", "prompt": "No one in the French department to which Professor Alban belongs is allowed to teach more than one introductory level class in any one term. Moreover, the only language classes being taught next term are advanced ones. So it is untrue that both of the French classes Professor Alban will be teaching next term will be introductory level classes.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) There is a rule. · It applies to a French department. · Professor Alban belongs to it. · No one there may teach more than one introductory level class. · The limit is per term. (2) This is a second premise. · It is about next term. · The only language classes being taught are advanced ones. (3) This is the conclusion. · It denies a claim. · The claim is about two French classes. · Professor Alban will teach them next term. · The claim is that both will be introductory level.", "category": "Parallel Reasoning", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "No one in the French department to which Professor Alban belongs is allowed to teach more than one introductory level class in any one term.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "There is a rule."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It applies to a French department."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Professor Alban belongs to it."}, {"n": 4, "text": "No one there may teach more than one introductory level class."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The limit is per term."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Moreover, the only language classes being taught next term are advanced ones.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a second premise."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about next term."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The only language classes being taught are advanced ones."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "So it is untrue that both of the French classes Professor Alban will be teaching next term will be introductory level classes.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It denies a claim."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The claim is about two French classes."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Professor Alban will teach them next term."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The claim is that both will be introductory level."}]}], "the_read": "What if Professor Alban is teaching a language class at a different school next term?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q19", "qnum": 19, "question_type": "Parallel Reasoning", "correct_answer": "D"}]}, {"order": 19, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q20", "prompt": "Some people have been promoting a new herbal mixture as a remedy for the common cold. The mixture contains, among other things, extracts of the plants purple coneflower and goldenseal. A cold sufferer, skeptical of the claim that the mixture is an effective cold remedy, argued, \"Suppose that the mixture were an effective cold remedy. Since most people with colds wish to recover quickly, it follows that almost everybody with a cold would be using it. Therefore, since there are many people who have colds but do not use the mixture, it is obviously not effective.\"", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Some people are promoting something. · What they promote is a herbal mixture. · The mixture is new. · They promote it as a remedy. · The remedy is for the common cold. (2) The mixture contains extracts. · The extracts are of plants. · One plant is purple coneflower. · The other is goldenseal. · It contains other things too. (3) A cold sufferer makes an argument. · The sufferer is skeptical. · The skepticism is about the claim that the mixture is an effective cold remedy. · The argument opens with a supposition. · The supposition is that the mixture were effective. (4) This is a premise. · Most people with colds wish to recover quickly. · A consequence is drawn from it. · Almost everybody with a cold would be using it. (5) This is the conclusion. · There are many people who have colds. · Those people do not use the mixture. · The mixture is not effective. · The speaker treats this as obvious.", "category": "Necessary Assumption", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Some people have been promoting a new herbal mixture as a remedy for the common cold.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Some people are promoting something."}, {"n": 2, "text": "What they promote is a herbal mixture."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The mixture is new."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They promote it as a remedy."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The remedy is for the common cold."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "The mixture contains, among other things, extracts of the plants purple coneflower and goldenseal.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The mixture contains extracts."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The extracts are of plants."}, {"n": 3, "text": "One plant is purple coneflower."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The other is goldenseal."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It contains other things too."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "A cold sufferer, skeptical of the claim that the mixture is an effective cold remedy, argued, \"Suppose that the mixture were an effective cold remedy.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "A cold sufferer makes an argument."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The sufferer is skeptical."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The skepticism is about the claim that the mixture is an effective cold remedy."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The argument opens with a supposition."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The supposition is that the mixture were effective."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Since most people with colds wish to recover quickly, it follows that almost everybody with a cold would be using it.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a premise."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Most people with colds wish to recover quickly."}, {"n": 3, "text": "A consequence is drawn from it."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Almost everybody with a cold would be using it."}]}, {"n": 5, "text": "Therefore, since there are many people who have colds but do not use the mixture, it is obviously not effective.\"", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There are many people who have colds."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those people do not use the mixture."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The mixture is not effective."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The speaker treats this as obvious."}]}], "the_read": "What if very few people know about the remedy? What if there are other, better, more widely known remedies?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q20", "qnum": 20, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "C"}, {"citation": "PT105.S2.Q21", "qnum": 21, "question_type": "Method", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 20, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q22", "prompt": "To hold criminals responsible for their crimes involves a failure to recognize that criminal actions, like all actions, are ultimately products of the environment that forged the agent''s character. It is not criminals but people in the law-abiding majority who by their actions do most to create and maintain this environment. Therefore, it is law-abiding people whose actions, and nothing else, make them alone truly responsible for crime.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about holding criminals responsible. · They are held responsible for their crimes. · Doing so involves a failure. · The failure is to recognize something. · What is not recognized concerns criminal actions. (2) Criminal actions are like all actions. · They are products of the environment. · This is ultimately so. · The environment forged the agent''s character. (3) Criminals are not the ones who do most. · The ones who do are people in the law-abiding majority. · They do it by their actions. · What they do most is create and maintain this environment. (4) This is the conclusion. · It is about law-abiding people. · Their actions make them responsible. · Nothing other than their actions does. · They alone are responsible. · The responsibility is true responsibility. · It is responsibility for crime.", "category": "Classic Flaw", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "To hold criminals responsible for their crimes involves a failure to recognize that criminal actions,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about holding criminals responsible."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They are held responsible for their crimes."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Doing so involves a failure."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The failure is to recognize something."}, {"n": 5, "text": "What is not recognized concerns criminal actions."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "like all actions, are ultimately products of the environment that forged the agent''s character.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Criminal actions are like all actions."}, {"n": 2, "text": "They are products of the environment."}, {"n": 3, "text": "This is ultimately so."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The environment forged the agent''s character."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "It is not criminals but people in the law-abiding majority who by their actions do most to create and maintain this environment.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Criminals are not the ones who do most."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The ones who do are people in the law-abiding majority."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They do it by their actions."}, {"n": 4, "text": "What they do most is create and maintain this environment."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Therefore, it is law-abiding people whose actions, and nothing else, make them alone truly responsible for crime.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is about law-abiding people."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Their actions make them responsible."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Nothing other than their actions does."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They alone are responsible."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The responsibility is true responsibility."}, {"n": 7, "text": "It is responsibility for crime."}]}], "the_read": "What if just because someone is a product of their environment, that doesn''t mean their environment is solely responsible for everything they do?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q22", "qnum": 22, "question_type": "Classic Flaw", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 21, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q23", "prompt": "Chronic back pain is usually caused by a herniated or degenerated spinal disk. In most cases the disk will have been damaged years before chronic pain develops, and in fact an estimated one in five people over the age of 30 has a herniated or degenerated disk that shows no chronic symptoms. If chronic pain later develops in such a case, it is generally brought about by a deterioration of the abdominal and spinal muscles caused by insufficient exercise.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This is about chronic back pain. · It usually has one cause. · The cause is a spinal disk. · The disk is herniated or degenerated. (2) This is true in most cases. · The disk was damaged earlier. · The damage came years earlier. · It came before the chronic pain developed. (3) This is an estimate. · It is one in five people. · Those people are over the age of 30. · They have a herniated or degenerated disk. · That disk shows no chronic symptoms. (4) This is conditional on chronic pain developing later. · It concerns such a case. · The pain is generally brought about by a deterioration. · The deterioration is of muscles. · The muscles are abdominal and spinal. · The deterioration is caused by insufficient exercise.", "category": "Most Strongly Supported", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Chronic back pain is usually caused by a herniated or degenerated spinal disk.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about chronic back pain."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It usually has one cause."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The cause is a spinal disk."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The disk is herniated or degenerated."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "In most cases the disk will have been damaged years before chronic pain develops,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is true in most cases."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The disk was damaged earlier."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The damage came years earlier."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It came before the chronic pain developed."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "and in fact an estimated one in five people over the age of 30 has a herniated or degenerated disk that shows no chronic symptoms.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is an estimate."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is one in five people."}, {"n": 3, "text": "Those people are over the age of 30."}, {"n": 4, "text": "They have a herniated or degenerated disk."}, {"n": 5, "text": "That disk shows no chronic symptoms."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "If chronic pain later develops in such a case, it is generally brought about by a deterioration of the abdominal and spinal muscles caused by insufficient exercise.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is conditional on chronic pain developing later."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It concerns such a case."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The pain is generally brought about by a deterioration."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The deterioration is of muscles."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The muscles are abdominal and spinal."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The deterioration is caused by insufficient exercise."}]}], "the_read": "People may be able to take actions that prevent herniated or degenerated disks from becoming painful.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q23", "qnum": 23, "question_type": "Most Strongly Supported", "correct_answer": "E"}]}, {"order": 22, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q24", "prompt": "Each December 31 in Country Q, a tally is made of the country''s total available coal supplies—that is, the total amount of coal that has been mined throughout the country but not consumed. In 1991 that amount was considerably lower than it had been in 1990. Furthermore, Country Q has not imported or exported coal since 1970.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) This happens each December 31. · The place is Country Q. · A tally is made. · The tally is of total available coal supplies. · They are the country''s. · A definition of that term follows. (2) This is the definition. · It is the total amount of coal. · The coal has been mined. · It was mined throughout the country. · The coal has not been consumed. (3) This is about 1991. · The amount was lower. · It was considerably lower than in 1990. (4) This is an additional fact. · Country Q has not imported coal. · It has not exported coal. · This has held since 1970.", "category": "Inference", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Each December 31 in Country Q, a tally is made of the country''s total available coal supplies—that is,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This happens each December 31."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The place is Country Q."}, {"n": 3, "text": "A tally is made."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The tally is of total available coal supplies."}, {"n": 5, "text": "They are the country''s."}, {"n": 6, "text": "A definition of that term follows."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "the total amount of coal that has been mined throughout the country but not consumed.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is the definition."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It is the total amount of coal."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The coal has been mined."}, {"n": 4, "text": "It was mined throughout the country."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The coal has not been consumed."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "In 1991 that amount was considerably lower than it had been in 1990.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is about 1991."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The amount was lower."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It was considerably lower than in 1990."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Furthermore, Country Q has not imported or exported coal since 1970.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is an additional fact."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Country Q has not imported coal."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It has not exported coal."}, {"n": 4, "text": "This has held since 1970."}]}], "the_read": "More coal was consumed than was mined in 1991 in Country Q.", "the_read_type": "I", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q24", "qnum": 24, "question_type": "Inference", "correct_answer": "B"}]}, {"order": 23, "slug": "PT105_S2_Q25", "prompt": "Tom: Employers complain that people graduating from high school too often lack the vocational skills required for full-time employment. Therefore, since these skills are best acquired on the job, we should require high school students to work at part-time jobs so that they acquire the skills needed for today''s job market.\n\nMary: There are already too few part-time jobs for students who want to work, and simply requiring students to work will not create jobs for them.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Tom is the first speaker. · Employers are making a complaint. · The complaint is about people graduating from high school. · Those people lack vocational skills. · The skills are required for full-time employment. · This happens too often. (2) This begins his conclusion. · It rests on a premise. · The premise is that these skills are best acquired on the job. (3) This is his recommendation. · High school students should be required to work. · The work is part-time jobs. · The purpose is that they acquire skills. · The skills are needed for today''s job market. (4) Mary is the second speaker. · There are already too few part-time jobs. · They are too few for students who want to work. · Simply requiring students to work will not create jobs. · It will not create jobs for them.", "category": "Method", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Tom: Employers complain that people graduating from high school too often lack the vocational skills required for full-time employment.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Tom is the first speaker."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Employers are making a complaint."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The complaint is about people graduating from high school."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Those people lack vocational skills."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The skills are required for full-time employment."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This happens too often."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "Therefore, since these skills are best acquired on the job,", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This begins his conclusion."}, {"n": 2, "text": "It rests on a premise."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The premise is that these skills are best acquired on the job."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "we should require high school students to work at part-time jobs so that they acquire the skills needed for today''s job market.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is his recommendation."}, {"n": 2, "text": "High school students should be required to work."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The work is part-time jobs."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The purpose is that they acquire skills."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The skills are needed for today''s job market."}]}, {"n": 4, "text": "Mary: There are already too few part-time jobs for students who want to work, and simply requiring students to work will not create jobs for them.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Mary is the second speaker."}, {"n": 2, "text": "There are already too few part-time jobs."}, {"n": 3, "text": "They are too few for students who want to work."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Simply requiring students to work will not create jobs."}, {"n": 5, "text": "It will not create jobs for them."}]}], "the_read": "The speakers disagree over whether high school students should be required to work part time.", "the_read_type": "C", "questions": [{"citation": "PT105.S2.Q25", "qnum": 25, "question_type": "Method", "correct_answer": "D"}]}]'::jsonb,
