"}, {"n": 5, "text": "At least the basics are required."}, {"n": 6, "text": "This is the conclusion."}, {"n": 7, "text": "Some books published by Garden Path are flawed."}]}], "the_read": "What if an explanation of the basics of composting doesn''t need to include an explanation of the difference between hot and cold composting?", "the_read_type": "L", "questions": [{"citation": "PT134.S3.Q12", "qnum": 12, "question_type": "Necessary Assumption", "correct_answer": "C"}]}, {"order": 13, "slug": "PT134_S3_Q13", "prompt": "Astronomers have found new evidence that the number of galaxies in the universe is not 10 billion, as previously believed, but 50 billion. This discovery will have an important effect on theories about how galaxies are formed. But even though astronomers now believe 40 billion more galaxies exist, many astronomers'' estimates of the universe''s total mass remain virtually unchanged.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) Astronomers have found evidence. · The evidence is new. · It concerns the number of galaxies in the universe. · The number was previously believed to be 10 billion. · The number is not that. · The number is 50 billion. (2) The discovery will have an effect. · The effect is important. · The effect is on theories. · Those theories concern how galaxies are formed. (3) This is a contrast. · Astronomers now believe more galaxies exist. · The additional number is 40 billion. · Many astronomers make estimates. · The estimates are of the universe''s total mass. · Those estimates remain unchanged. · They are virtually unchanged.", "category": "Resolution", "chunks": [{"n": 1, "text": "Astronomers have found new evidence that the number of galaxies in the universe is not 10 billion, as previously believed, but 50 billion.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "Astronomers have found evidence."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The evidence is new."}, {"n": 3, "text": "It concerns the number of galaxies in the universe."}, {"n": 4, "text": "The number was previously believed to be 10 billion."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The number is not that."}, {"n": 6, "text": "The number is 50 billion."}]}, {"n": 2, "text": "This discovery will have an important effect on theories about how galaxies are formed.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "The discovery will have an effect."}, {"n": 2, "text": "The effect is important."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The effect is on theories."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Those theories concern how galaxies are formed."}]}, {"n": 3, "text": "But even though astronomers now believe 40 billion more galaxies exist, many astronomers'' estimates of the universe''s total mass remain virtually unchanged.", "details": [{"n": 1, "text": "This is a contrast."}, {"n": 2, "text": "Astronomers now believe more galaxies exist."}, {"n": 3, "text": "The additional number is 40 billion."}, {"n": 4, "text": "Many astronomers make estimates."}, {"n": 5, "text": "The estimates are of the universe''s total mass."}, {"n": 6, "text": "Those estimates remain unchanged."}, {"n": 7, "text": "They are virtually unchanged."}]}], "the_read": "What if galaxy mass is a negligible amount of the entire universe''s mass? What if astronomers now believe each galaxy has a much smaller mass than previously thought?", "the_read_type": "R", "questions": [{"citation": "PT134.S3.Q13", "qnum": 13, "question_type": "Resolution", "correct_answer": "A"}]}, {"order": 14, "slug": "PT134_S3_Q14", "prompt": "Newspaper subscriber: Arnot''s editorial argues that by making certain fundamental changes in government we would virtually eliminate our most vexing social ills. But clearly this conclusion is false. After all, the argument Arnot makes for this claim depends on the dubious assumption that government can be trusted to act in the interest of the public.", "credited_answers": [], "cumulative_after": [], "explanation": "The details your recall has to carry, by chunk: (1) A newspaper subscriber is 